{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07Y6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nB' \\ar[r] & B \\\\\nA' \\ar[u] \\ar[r] & A \\ar[u]\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0010": "$y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Spec(B)$", "MATH_0013": "$\\phi : f(x)|_{\\Spec(B)} \\to y$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Spec(B)$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\textit{Lift}(x, A') \\longrightarrow \\textit{Lift}(y, B')\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$f$", "MATH_0018": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0019": "$1$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-functoriality}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eaf6b94da36feb1884bbe3b00e39a30063f76046ed2475053b7097b87511a465", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:acc420e98108c0bc71419f73a328bcd303854dec82c066d0acf18e8ace707dc8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a <MATH_0003>-morphism\nof categories fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0004>. Let\n<MATH_0005>\nbe a commutative diagram of <MATH_0006>-algebras. Let <MATH_0007> be an object of <MATH_0008>\nover <MATH_0009>, let <MATH_0010> be an object of <MATH_0011> over <MATH_0012>,\nand let <MATH_0013> be a morphism of <MATH_0014>\nover <MATH_0015>. Then there is a canonical functor\n<MATH_0016>\nof categories of lifts induced by <MATH_0017> and <MATH_0018>. The construction is\ncompatible with compositions of <MATH_0019>-morphisms of categories fibred in\ngroupoids in an obvious manner.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e51d7e72f7b75bc5538745636ec9f1afaa253c27ff83291f13c1d7a3a2d7e8fd", "unit_id": "tag:07Y7:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "07Y6", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c06ac3e28f5d2da9fc574767aa85267f8f6bef04a986ed6c5d59bbb3e550880e", "source_text": "This lemma proves itself.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be208ed8d1d8086544c0a3e82046286f19a92607ac3c5e6fa1a30dd84b0dad32", "unit_id": "tag:07Y7:proof"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07Y6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$(x, A' \\to A)$", "MATH_0005": "$A' \\to A$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0010": "$(y, B' \\to B) \\to (x, A' \\to A)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nB' \\ar[r] & B \\\\\nA' \\ar[u] \\ar[r] & A \\ar[u]\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "MATH_0013": "$x|_{\\Spec(B)} \\to y$", "MATH_0014": "$\\Spec(B)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09f2bfa1ef853e6a32b9667515aae9a587a11822a3810d824833705c53000363", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54d7233892831accfd5e2f9384165a8f68abbd410b92c3ad2284ac2d290c0db0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a base scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category fibred\nin groupoids over <MATH_0003>. We define a category whose objects are\npairs <MATH_0004> where\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is a surjection of <MATH_0006>-algebras whose kernel\nis an ideal of square zero,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is an object of <MATH_0008> lying over <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nA morphism <MATH_0010> is given by a commutative\ndiagram\n<MATH_0011>\nof <MATH_0012>-algebras together with a morphism <MATH_0013> over\n<MATH_0014>. Let us call this the category of <TEXTITOPEN_0001>deformation situations<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:916b843cd9e870aa3277907eafdde8c747f512485ba7c816a4d87908cb9debcc", "unit_id": "tag:07Y6:prose-0002"}
